        <li>Find what you are genuinely hungry for, beneath the noise of everything you are "supposed" to want</li>
        <li>Say a clear, guilt-free no, even in the situations where you cannot simply walk away</li>
        <li>Break the grip of comparison by curating what you allow into your head</li>
        <li>Protect your attention in a world engineered to fragment it</li>
        <li>Trade the frictionless comfort of screens for the messy, meaningful friction of real people and real life</li>
        <li>Choose "one-thing seasons" and go deep, instead of skimming the surface of a dozen half-finished projects</li>
        <li>Turn a life that is merely full into one that is genuinely fulfilling</li>
      </ul>
